h India, AED 15-45K GCC). Enterprise upper (Rs 10-30 lakh India, AED 45-150K GCC). Rule: 25-35% of monthly revenue launch validation, 15-25% scaling, 8-15% mature. Peak season (Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism) concentrates 45-65% annual ad budget in 12-16 weeks. Wedding + festive brands see 60-80% concentration in Oct-March India."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Meta vs Snapchat vs TikTok for fashion in Oman?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Same country breakdowns as perfume — India Meta + Instagram + Reels dominant, UAE trilingual + Snapchat 15-25%, KSA Snapchat 40-50% dominant. For fashion specifically, TikTok growing 25-40% YoY across markets — native-first content on TikTok (not repurposed Reels), TikTok Shop integration + Spark Ads amplification. Pinterest under-utilised for fashion — strongest for wedding + occasion + ethnic + wedding-guest + gift-planning. Higher-intent than Instagram + TikTok for occasion planning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do fashion ads need Arabic + regional-language creative in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Same principle as perfume — India regional-language adds 25-40% CPL efficiency for regional catchment; GCC trilingual (Arabic + English + Hindi) mandatory. For Muscat with Arabic + English + Hindi + Malayalam + Urdu + Baluchi + Swahili, native-speaker outperforms English-only 30-50%. Fashion specifically needs Arabic-native for KSA modest fashion + abaya + wedding sub-verticals — non-negotiable."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What role does influencer + creator play in fashion social?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Essential — fashion is aspiration + validation + trust-driven. Micro (10-100K, best ROI, OMR 5-40K/post) + macro (100K-1M, OMR 30K-2 lakh/post) + celebrity + stylist (Rina Shah + Ami Patel tier + Bollywood OMR 5-50 lakh/campaign). UGC rights + Meta Branded Content Partner essential. Fashion sub-vertical creator network: streetwear (skate + gaming + music + comedy), menswear (lifestyle + fitness + finfluencer), womenswear (beauty + fashion + stylist), ethnic + wedding (wedding photographer + stylist + bridal magazine + Bollywood), sustainable (climate + minimalist + YouTube + PR), modest + GCC (Muslim + Arabic-native)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we set up attribution + CAPI for fashion social?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Meta CAPI (recovers 15-25% attribution) essential. Google Enhanced Conversions API. WhatsApp CTWA click tracking. LTV/CAC/cohort dashboard weekly. Value-based bidding (Meta Advantage+ Shopping + Google PMax with LTV-weighted goals). Fashion-specific: subscription + rental + repeat cohort tracking, drop + collab attribution, marketplace + D2C attribution split. Triple Whale + Northbeam typical fashion attribution stack. In Muscat with Omani + South Asian expat (Kerala + Baluchistan heritage) + East African + Arab expat, custom UTM structure for Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism campaigns."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we control ad fatigue for fashion social in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Creative velocity is #1 defence. Boutique 4-8/week, Growth 15-30/week, Enterprise 30-80/week (streetwear + drops especially). Additional defences: audience expansion + lookalike refresh 2-4 weeks, creative refresh 3-4 weeks, frequency cap 3-5 impressions/week, exclude converted customers from prospecting, creator UGC injection retargeting, drop + collab + seasonal campaigns disrupt fatigue. In Muscat peak seasons (Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism) creative fatigue slows because audience expands + intent is high."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Peak-season spend concentration for fashion in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Muscat fashion peaks: Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism. 45-65% annual ad spend in 12-16 peak weeks. Pre-peak (8-10 weeks): baseline + audience-building. Peak (4-6 weeks): 2-4x baseline spend + creative-velocity spike. Post-peak (2-4 weeks): retention + winback. India Oct-Feb wedding + Diwali = fashion's biggest peak. GCC Ramadan + Eid + DSF = biggest peak. Off-peak (June-July India, post-Eid GCC) = 60-70% of peak daily spend."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should we optimise for first-purchase vs LTV bidding for fashion?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"LTV-weighted wins by month 6+. First-purchase CPA looks good short-term but compresses margin + limits scale. LTV-weighted: Meta Advantage+ Shopping value-based + Google PMax + Value Bidding + manual bid caps on cohort LTV. Fashion typical 12-month LTV: streetwear OMR 3-8K, menswear premium OMR 6-18K, womenswear OMR 5-25K, ethnic + wedding OMR 10-100K, sustainable OMR 8-30K. First-purchase optimisation only for launch validation, brand-search, new-buyer isolation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does ITD GrowthLabs manage fashion social in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Full-stack: channel mix per Oman (Meta + Snapchat + TikTok + WhatsApp CTWA + Pinterest for occasion), creative production (in-house pod 15-30 units/week for Growth, 30-80/week for Enterprise streetwear), trilingual creative GCC, sub-vertical creator programme, CAPI + Enhanced Conversions + attribution + LTV/CAC/cohort reporting, drop + collab + peak-season campaigns. Grounded in ITD's fashion vertical + case studies (Snitch + Bewakoof + Libas + Urbanic + The Souled Store + Bombay Shirt Company + FabIndia (India); Namshi + Modanisa + local D2C emerging (GCC)). Retainer starts at OMR 450-2,000 + ad spend separate. See Digital Marketing for Fashion + Apparel Brands ."}}]}</script>
